course: dictionary
lesson: 6434
title: Strange and magical words
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Mystical is an adjective. It describes something that feels strange, magical and full of wonder, as if it belongs to a world beyond the everyday one. Writers use it when a scene seems holy or hard to explain.
explain: Read the words around the word for clues. «This is the book's mystical scene: the author tells of a holy, wonderful meeting, as a story, without ever naming the Piper.» Holy and wonderful are clues that the scene is spiritual and full of wonder, so mystical must mean strange, magical and wonderful.
explain: In The Wind in the Willows, the chapter «The Piper at the Gates of Dawn» is mystical. Rat and Mole meet the god Pan on an island and feel awe. Awe is a deep feeling of wonder, so you can see how the feeling in the scene helps you understand the word.
fact: Mystical is an adjective: it describes a noun, such as a mystical experience or a mystical light.
fact: Mystical means having a hidden spiritual meaning that is hard to explain, beyond the everyday world.
fact: Mystical also means strange, magical and full of wonder.
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, the chapter «The Piper at the Gates of Dawn» is mystical: Rat and Mole meet the god Pan on an island and feel awe.
fact: Awe is a feeling of great wonder, often mixed with respect.
exercise: «This is the book's mystical scene.» In this sentence, what does mystical mean? | Very noisy and busy | Wet and grey | Dull and ordinary | *Strange, magical and full of wonder
exercise: Rat and Mole meet the god Pan on an island and feel awe. Which feeling fits a mystical scene best? | *Awe, a deep sense of wonder | Anger | Boredom
exercise: Find and copy one word from «the author tells of a holy, wonderful meeting» that hints the scene is spiritual. | tells | *holy | story | author
test: The sky glowed with a mystical light. What does mystical mean here? | Boring and plain | *Strange and magical, full of wonder | Loud and busy | Very cold and wet
test: Which word could replace mystical in «a mystical experience» with almost the same meaning? | Sleepy | Noisy | *Spiritual | Tasty
exam: Which is the best way to explain mystical to a friend? | It means the same as ordinary | It means very fast | *It means strange and magical, with a hidden meaning that is hard to explain | It means a kind of food
